<title>BRAZIL: Bradesco says still eyes Brazil's Banerj.</title>
<headline>Bradesco says still eyes Brazil's Banerj.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian private bank Bradesco said on Thursday it is still interested in Rio de Janeiro state bank Banerj, despite the court orders which have been preventing the bank from being sold off.</p>
<p>Bradesco and Banco Itau were the only investors qualified to bid at Banerj's privatization auction, which was due to take place today but was suspended.</p>
<p>The auction was postponed for the second time after a judge ordered Banerj's assets should be re-evaluated. Banerj had been first scheduled to be sold off on December 17 but a court injunction granted to an association of the bank's employees blocked the sale.</p>
<p>Banerj was due to be the first of Brazilian state banks to be privatized.</p>
<p>((--Fatima Cristina Rio de Janeiro Newsroom 5521 5074151))</p>
